CVE-2026-59871: pax: parse values according to known types (GHSA-w8wr-v893-vjvp)

A PAX extended header entry such as `11 path=12345\n` caused the PAX key/value
parser to coerce a purely-numeric string value (e.g. a path or linkpath) into a
JavaScript number. Downstream code then treats these fields as strings (calling
String methods like substring/replace), producing a type-confusion crash in
strict mode or a failed extraction in non-strict mode.

Fix: parse PAX values according to a fixed allow-list of known keys and their
expected types (strings stay strings, time fields become Dates, numeric metadata
fields become numbers); unknown keys are ignored. As defense-in-depth, any value
flowing through normalizeWindowsPath is explicitly cast to String.

Applied AFTER CVE-2026-59874: that patch inserts an early `size < 0` reject in
pax.js; this patch replaces that block plus the old coerce-all-digits logic with
the typed switch (size keeps the non-negative check).

This patch targets the compiled dist/ files shipped in the npm tarball
(the published package contains no TypeScript sources).

